<span id="A7.SS3.p3.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p3.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">"related_correct_expressions": [
<br class="ltx_break"></span></span>
<span id="A7.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<span id="A7.Ex78"><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\frac{\partial L}{\partial r}=mr\dot{\theta}^{2}-\frac{k}{r^{2}}+\frac{k^{\prime}}{r^{3}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∂</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi></mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∂</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">˙</mo></mover><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\frac{\partial L}{\partial r}=mr\dot{\theta}^{2}-\frac{k}{r^{2}}+\frac{k^{\prime}}{r^{3}},</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
<span id="A7.Ex79"><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad m\ddot{r}=mr\dot{\theta}^{2}-\frac{k}{r^{2}}+\frac{k^{\prime}}{r^{3}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">¨</mo></mover></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">˙</mo></mover><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad m\ddot{r}=mr\dot{\theta}^{2}-\frac{k}{r^{2}}+\frac{k^{\prime}}{r^{3}}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A7.SS3.p3.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p3.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> ],
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:5.0pt;"><span id="A7.SS3.p3.pic1.2.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif">
</span></span></span>
<span id="A7.SS3.p3.pic1.2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p3.pic1.2.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">"rationale": "The student made a sign/algebra error when differentiating the potential terms in L with respect to r, flipping the signs of the k and k’ contributions. This is a pure derivation/computation mistake (not a misapplication of physics), since the correct radial equation has the opposite signs and follows from the correctly differentiated Lagrangian or directly from Newton’s form. The later orbit derivation uses the correct form of F(r), so the error is localized to the symbolic differentiation step."<span id="A7.SS3.p3.pic1.2.7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif">
</span></span></span><pre id="A7.SS3.p3.pic1.2.8" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">}
</pre>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="1616.08" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 1616.08" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,1616.08) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#B02418;" fill="#B02418" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.74 L 0 1611.34 C 0 1613.96 2.12 1616.08 4.74 1616.08 L 545.26 1616.08 C 547.88 1616.08 550 1613.96 550 1611.34 L 550 4.74 C 550 2.12 547.88 0 545.26 0 L 4.74 0 C 2.12 0 0 2.12 0 4.74 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F8E6EA;" fill="#F8E6EA" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 4.74 L 1.97 1575.36 L 548.03 1575.36 L 548.03 4.74 C 548.03 3.21 546.79 1.97 545.26 1.97 L 4.74 1.97 C 3.21 1.97 1.97 3.21 1.97 4.74 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#E197A8;" fill="#E197A8" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 1577.33 L 1.97 1611.34 C 1.97 1612.87 3.21 1614.11 4.74 1614.11 L 545.26 1614.11 C 546.79 1614.11 548.03 1612.87 548.03 1611.34 L 548.03 1577.33 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 12.82 1583.96)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:32.96em;--ltx-fo-height:1.89em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="28.9" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 26.21)" width="456.07"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:32.96em;">
<span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">PRISM-Physics<span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright"> Failure Example: Modeling and Process Understanding Error</span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 12.82 16.28)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.1em;--ltx-fo-height:111.89em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="1551.7" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 1548.24)" width="499.52"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.1em;">
<span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Problem: <span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">A particle of mass <math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> moves under a restoring force <math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-Kx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-Kx</annotation></semantics></math> and a resistive force <math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-Rv" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-Rv</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> is the displacement from equilibrium and <math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> is the particle’s velocity. Here, <math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> is the mass of the particle, <math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> is the spring constant, <math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> is the damping coefficient, <math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> is the displacement from equilibrium, and <math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> is the velocity. For fixed <math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> and arbitrary initial conditions, find the value <math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R=R_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R=R_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> that gives the most rapid approach to equilibrium. Also, state whether it is possible to choose initial conditions (other than <math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v=0</annotation></semantics></math>) such that the approach to equilibrium is more rapid for <math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R&gt;R_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R&gt;R_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R&lt;R_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R&lt;R_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>. Specifically, <math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> should be defined in terms of <math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>. Express the rate of approach and clearly specify all variables throughout. The final answer for the most rapid approach value should be given as <math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{c}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{c}=</annotation></semantics></math> in terms of <math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>.
<br class="ltx_break"></span></span></span>
<span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">GoundTruth Solution: 
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:5.0pt;"><span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
The equation of motion for the particle can be written as</span></span></span>
<span id="A7.Ex80" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\frac{d^{2}x}{dt^{2}}+R\frac{dx}{dt}+Kx=0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\frac{d^{2}x}{dt^{2}}+R\frac{dx}{dt}+Kx=0</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">……</span></span>
<span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Thus, for certain special (non-generic) initial conditions, the approach to equilibrium may be even faster than in the critically damped case.If <math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R&lt;R_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R&lt;R_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>, the roots are complex:</span></span>
<span id="A7.Ex81" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex81.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=\frac{-R\pm i\sqrt{R_{c}^{2}-R^{2}}}{2m}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">±</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=\frac{-R\pm i\sqrt{R_{c}^{2}-R^{2}}}{2m}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The general solution is</span></span>
<span id="A7.Ex82" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=A\exp\left(-\frac{Rt}{2m}\right)\cos\left(\frac{\sqrt{R_{c}^{2}-R^{2}}}{2m}t\right)+B\exp\left(-\frac{Rt}{2m}\right)\sin\left(\frac{\sqrt{R_{c}^{2}-R^{2}}}{2m}t\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=A\exp\left(-\frac{Rt}{2m}\right)\cos\left(\frac{\sqrt{R_{c}^{2}-R^{2}}}{2m}t\right)+B\exp\left(-\frac{Rt}{2m}\right)\sin\left(\frac{\sqrt{R_{c}^{2}-R^{2}}}{2m}t\right)</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The rate of decay towards equilibrium is determined by the exponential factor</span></span>
<span id="A7.Ex83" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex83.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{R}{2m}&lt;\frac{R_{c}}{2m}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></msub><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{R}{2m}&lt;\frac{R_{c}}{2m}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Thus, the approach to equilibrium is always slower than for critical damping when <math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R&lt;R_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R&lt;R_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>.
In summary, the value of <math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> that gives the most rapid approach to equilibrium for arbitrary initial conditions is</span></span>
<span id="A7.Ex84" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex84.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{c}=2\sqrt{Km}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{c}=2\sqrt{Km}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.8.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">For <math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R&gt;R_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R&gt;R_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>, in principle, one can choose initial conditions such that the approach is even more rapid, but this occurs only for special initial conditions (such as setting <math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=0</annotation></semantics></math> in the overdamped general solution). In general, for arbitrary initial conditions, critical damping (<math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R=R_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R=R_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>) gives the most rapid approach. For <math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R&lt;R_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R&lt;R_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>, the approach to equilibrium is always slower than for critical damping.
<br class="ltx_break"></span></span>
<span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Student Solution Snippet:
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:5.0pt;"><span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
The equation of motion for a damped harmonic oscillator is:</span></span></span>
<span id="A7.Ex85" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex85.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\frac{d^{2}x}{dt^{2}}=-Kx-R\frac{dx}{dt}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\frac{d^{2}x}{dt^{2}}=-Kx-R\frac{dx}{dt}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.10.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Rearranging to standard form:</span></span>
<span id="A7.Ex86" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex86.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d^{2}x}{dt^{2}}+\frac{R}{m}\frac{dx}{dt}+\frac{K}{m}x=0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d^{2}x}{dt^{2}}+\frac{R}{m}\frac{dx}{dt}+\frac{K}{m}x=0</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.11.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Let <math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{0}^{2}=\frac{K}{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ω</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{0}^{2}=\frac{K}{m}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\gamma=\frac{R}{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\gamma=\frac{R}{m}</annotation></semantics></math>, so the equation becomes:</span></span>
<span id="A7.Ex87" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex87.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d^{2}x}{dt^{2}}+2\gamma\frac{dx}{dt}+\omega_{0}^{2}x=0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ω</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d^{2}x}{dt^{2}}+2\gamma\frac{dx}{dt}+\omega_{0}^{2}x=0</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.12.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The characteristic equation is:</span></span>
<span id="A7.Ex88" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex88.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{2}+2\gamma r+\omega_{0}^{2}=0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ω</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{2}+2\gamma r+\omega_{0}^{2}=0</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.13" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.13.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The roots are:</span></span>
<span id="A7.Ex89" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex89.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=-\gamma\pm\sqrt{\gamma^{2}-\omega_{0}^{2}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">±</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ω</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=-\gamma\pm\sqrt{\gamma^{2}-\omega_{0}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.14" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.14.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The behavior depends on the discriminant <math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma^{2}-\omega_{0}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ω</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma^{2}-\omega_{0}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>:
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.14.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Case 1: Underdamped</span> (<math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&lt;\omega_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ω</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&lt;\omega_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R&lt;2\sqrt{Km}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R&lt;2\sqrt{Km}</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></span>
<span id="A7.Ex90" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex90.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x(t)=e^{-\gamma t}(A\cos(\omega_{d}t)+B\sin(\omega_{d}t))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ω</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ω</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x(t)=e^{-\gamma t}(A\cos(\omega_{d}t)+B\sin(\omega_{d}t))</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.15" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.15.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">where <math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{d}=\sqrt{\omega_{0}^{2}-\gamma^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ω</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ω</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{d}=\sqrt{\omega_{0}^{2}-\gamma^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.15.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Case 2: Critically damped</span> (<math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=\omega_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ω</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=\omega_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m37" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R=2\sqrt{Km}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R=2\sqrt{Km}</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></span>
<span id="A7.Ex91" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex91.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x(t)=e^{-\gamma t}(A+Bt)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x(t)=e^{-\gamma t}(A+Bt)</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.16" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.16.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Case 3: Overdamped<span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.16.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright"> (<math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m38" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&gt;\omega_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ω</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&gt;\omega_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m39" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R&gt;2\sqrt{Km}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R&gt;2\sqrt{Km}</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></span></span>
<span id="A7.Ex92" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex92.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x(t)=Ae^{r_{1}t}+Be^{r_{2}t}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x(t)=Ae^{r_{1}t}+Be^{r_{2}t}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.17" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.17.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">where <math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m40" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{1}=-\gamma+\sqrt{\gamma^{2}-\omega_{0}^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ω</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{1}=-\gamma+\sqrt{\gamma^{2}-\omega_{0}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m41" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{2}=-\gamma-\sqrt{\gamma^{2}-\omega_{0}^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ω</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{2}=-\gamma-\sqrt{\gamma^{2}-\omega_{0}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>.For the most rapid approach to equilibrium, we need to minimize the time for <math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m42" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x(t)\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x(t)\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
<span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.18" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.18.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">In the underdamped case, the envelope decays as <math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m43" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{-\gamma t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{-\gamma t}</annotation></semantics></math>.In the critically damped case, the decay is <math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m44" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{-\gamma t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{-\gamma t}</annotation></semantics></math>.In the overdamped case, the slowest decay rate is determined by <math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m45" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{1}=-\gamma+\sqrt{\gamma^{2}-\omega_{0}^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ω</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{1}=-\gamma+\sqrt{\gamma^{2}-\omega_{0}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>.Since <math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m46" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\gamma^{2}-\omega_{0}^{2}}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ω</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\gamma^{2}-\omega_{0}^{2}}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m47" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&gt;\omega_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ω</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&gt;\omega_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m48" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|r_{1}|&lt;\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|r_{1}|&lt;\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, making overdamped systems slower than critically damped.</span></span>
<span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.19" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.19.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">For underdamped systems, the envelope decay rate is <math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m49" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=\frac{R}{2m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=\frac{R}{2m}</annotation></semantics></math>.For critically damped systems, the decay rate is also <math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m50" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=\frac{R}{2m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=\frac{R}{2m}</annotation></semantics></math>.However, the critically damped case has no oscillations and provides the fastest approach without overshoot.Therefore, the critical damping condition gives the most rapid approach:</span></span>
<span id="A7.Ex93" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex93.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{c}=2\sqrt{Km}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{c}=2\sqrt{Km}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.20" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.20.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Regarding initial conditions: For any given <math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m51" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>, the approach rate is determined by the system parameters, not the initial conditions. The initial conditions only affect the amplitude coefficients <math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m52" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m53" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>, but not the fundamental decay rates. Therefore, it is <span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.20.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">not possible</span> to choose initial conditions to make <math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m54" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R&gt;R_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R&gt;R_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m55" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R&lt;R_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R&lt;R_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> approach equilibrium more rapidly than <math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m56" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R=R_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R=R_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
<span id="A7.Ex94" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex94.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{c}=2\sqrt{Km}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{c}=2\sqrt{Km}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.21" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.21.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Error Analysis Output:<span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.21.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span><pre id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.22" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
{
  "primary_error": "MPUE",
</pre>
<span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.23" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.23.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> "incorrect_expressions": [
"Therefore, it is not possible to choose initial conditions to make <math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m57" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R&gt;R_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R&gt;R_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m58" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R&lt;R_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R&lt;R_{c}</annotation></semantics></math> approach equilibrium more rapidly than <math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m59" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R=R_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R=R_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>.",
"However, the critically damped case has no oscillations and provides the fastest approach without overshoot."
],
<br class="ltx_break"></span></span>
<span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.24" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.24.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">"related_correct_expressions": [
</span></span>
<span id="A7.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<span id="A7.Ex95"><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex95.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad m\frac{d^{2}x}{dt^{2}}=-Kx-R\frac{dx}{dt}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad m\frac{d^{2}x}{dt^{2}}=-Kx-R\frac{dx}{dt},</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
<span id="A7.Ex96"><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex96.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad R_{c}=2\sqrt{Km}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad R_{c}=2\sqrt{Km},</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
<span id="A7.Ex97"><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex97.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad r=-\gamma\pm\sqrt{\gamma^{2}-\omega_{0}^{2}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">±</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ω</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad r=-\gamma\pm\sqrt{\gamma^{2}-\omega_{0}^{2}},</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
<span id="A7.Ex98"><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex98.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\text{Underdamped: }x(t)=e^{-\gamma t}(A\cos(\omega_{d}t)+B\sin(\omega_{d}t))," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">Underdamped: </mtext><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">cos</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ω</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi></msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">sin</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ω</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi></msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\text{Underdamped: }x(t)=e^{-\gamma t}(A\cos(\omega_{d}t)+B\sin(\omega_{d}t)),</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
<span id="A7.Ex99"><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex99.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\text{Critically damped: }x(t)=e^{-\gamma t}(A+Bt)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">Critically damped: </mtext><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\text{Critically damped: }x(t)=e^{-\gamma t}(A+Bt),</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
<span id="A7.Ex100"><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex100.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\text{Overdamped: }x(t)=Ae^{r_{1}t}+Be^{r_{2}t},\quad r_{1}=-\gamma+\sqrt{\gamma^{2}-\omega_{0}^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace" mathcolor="#000000">Overdamped: </mtext><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></mrow></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></mrow></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="1.167em">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">=</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ω</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\text{Overdamped: }x(t)=Ae^{r_{1}t}+Be^{r_{2}t},\quad r_{1}=-\gamma+\sqrt{\gamma^{2}-\omega_{0}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.25" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.25.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">

],
<span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.25.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif">
</span></span></span>
<span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.26" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.26.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">"rationale": "The student correctly derived the equation of motion , root structure, and critical damping value <math id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.m60" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{c}</annotation></semantics></math>, but then asserted that initial conditions cannot alter which R gives the fastest approach. That is a modelling process misunderstanding: transient approach time can depend on initial conditions (e.g. certain initial displacements or velocities can make overdamped underdamped responses reach zero sooner for some measures). The blanket statement that critical damping is always fastest for every initial condition is therefore incorrect."
<span id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.26.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif">
</span></span></span><pre id="A7.SS3.p4.pic1.2.27" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
}
</pre>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="944" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 944" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,944) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#B02418;" fill="#B02418" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.74 L 0 939.27 C 0 941.88 2.12 944 4.74 944 L 545.26 944 C 547.88 944 550 941.88 550 939.27 L 550 4.74 C 550 2.12 547.88 0 545.26 0 L 4.74 0 C 2.12 0 0 2.12 0 4.74 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F8E6EA;" fill="#F8E6EA" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 4.74 L 1.97 903.29 L 548.03 903.29 L 548.03 4.74 C 548.03 3.21 546.79 1.97 545.26 1.97 L 4.74 1.97 C 3.21 1.97 1.97 3.21 1.97 4.74 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#E197A8;" fill="#E197A8" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 905.26 L 1.97 939.27 C 1.97 940.8 3.21 942.04 4.74 942.04 L 545.26 942.04 C 546.79 942.04 548.03 940.8 548.03 939.27 L 548.03 905.26 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 12.82 911.89)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:32.96em;--ltx-fo-height:1.89em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="28.9" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 26.21)" width="456.07"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:32.96em;">
<span id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_smallcaps" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">PRISM-Physics<span id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright"> Failure Example: Physics Theorem Application Error</span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 12.82 16.28)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.1em;--ltx-fo-height:63.32em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="879.62" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 876.16)" width="499.52"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.1em;">
<span id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Problem<span id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">: A bucket of mass <math id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> (when empty) initially at rest and containing a mass of water is being pulled up a well by a rope exerting a steady force <math id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> The water is leaking out of the bucket at a steady rate such that the bucket is empty after a time <math id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝝉</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math> .Find the velocity of the bucket at the instant it becomes empty.
<br class="ltx_break"></span></span></span>
<span id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">GroundTruth Solution <span id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">: 
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:5.0pt;">
Let the total mass of the bucket and water at time <math id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> be <math id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span></span>
<span id="A7.Ex101" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex101.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\prime}=M+m-\frac{mt}{\tau}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\prime}=M+m-\frac{mt}{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The equation of motion for the bucket (plus remaining water) is</span></span>
<span id="A7.Ex102" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex102.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M^{\prime}\frac{dv}{dt}=P-M^{\prime}g" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">g</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M^{\prime}\frac{dv}{dt}=P-M^{\prime}g</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Rearranging gives</span></span>
<span id="A7.Ex103" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex103.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="dv=\left(\frac{P}{M+m-\frac{m}{\tau}t}-g\right)dt" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">g</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">dv=\left(\frac{P}{M+m-\frac{m}{\tau}t}-g\right)dt</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The velocity <math id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> of the bucket at time <math id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=\tau</annotation></semantics></math> (when empty) starting from rest is</span></span>
<span id="A7.Ex104" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex104.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{empty}=\int_{0}^{\tau}\frac{Pdt}{M+m-\frac{m}{\tau}t}-g\tau" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∫</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi></msubsup><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{empty}=\int_{0}^{\tau}\frac{Pdt}{M+m-\frac{m}{\tau}t}-g\tau</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Evaluating the integral yields</span></span>
<span id="A7.Ex105" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex105.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{empty}=\frac{P\tau}{m}\ln\left(\frac{M+m}{M}\right)-g\tau" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{empty}=\frac{P\tau}{m}\ln\left(\frac{M+m}{M}\right)-g\tau</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.2.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">where <math id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{empty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{empty}</annotation></semantics></math> is the velocity of the bucket at the instant it becomes empty.
<br class="ltx_break"></span></span>
<span id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.2.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Student Solution Snippet:
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:5.0pt;"><span id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.2.8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
I need to find the velocity of the bucket when it becomes empty at time <math id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=\tau</annotation></semantics></math>.
Setting up the problem
The mass of water decreases linearly from <math id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> over time <math id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></span></span>
<span id="A7.Ex106" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex106.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{water}(t)=m(1-\frac{t}{\tau})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{water}(t)=m(1-\frac{t}{\tau})</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.2.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.2.9.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The total mass of the system at time <math id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is:</span></span>
<span id="A7.Ex107" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex107.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{total}(t)=M+m(1-\frac{t}{\tau})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{total}(t)=M+m(1-\frac{t}{\tau})</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.2.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.2.10.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The rate of mass loss is:</span></span>
<span id="A7.Ex108" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex108.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{dm_{water}}{dt}=-\frac{m}{\tau}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{dm_{water}}{dt}=-\frac{m}{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.2.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.2.11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Applying Newton’s Second Law<span id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.2.11.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
<span id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.2.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.2.12.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Since the leaked water has zero velocity relative to the bucket, when it leaves the bucket, it has the same velocity <math id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> as the bucket. The forces acting on the system are:
<br class="ltx_break"> - Upward force: <math id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> - Weight: <math id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(M+m_{water}(t))g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">g</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(M+m_{water}(t))g</annotation></semantics></math>
<br class="ltx_break">Using Newton’s second law for variable mass systems:</span></span>
<span id="A7.Ex109" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex109.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P-(M+m(1-\frac{t}{\tau}))g=(M+m(1-\frac{t}{\tau}))\frac{dv}{dt}+v\frac{dm_{water}}{dt}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">g</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P-(M+m(1-\frac{t}{\tau}))g=(M+m(1-\frac{t}{\tau}))\frac{dv}{dt}+v\frac{dm_{water}}{dt}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.2.13" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.2.13.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">……</span></span>
<span id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.2.14" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.2.14.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Error Analysis Output:<span id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.2.14.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span><pre id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.2.15" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
\begin{verbatim}
{
 "primary_error": "PTAE",
</pre>
<span id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.2.16" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.2.16.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">"incorrect_expressions": [
<br class="ltx_break"></span></span>
<span id="A7.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<span id="A7.Ex110"><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex110.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad P-(M+m(1-\tfrac{t}{\tau}))g=(M+m(1-\tfrac{t}{\tau}))\tfrac{dv}{dt}+v\tfrac{dm_{water}}{dt}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">g</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad P-(M+m(1-\tfrac{t}{\tau}))g=(M+m(1-\tfrac{t}{\tau}))\tfrac{dv}{dt}+v\tfrac{dm_{water}}{dt}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.2.17" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.2.17.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> ],
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:5.0pt;"><span id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.2.17.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif">
</span></span></span>
<span id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.2.18" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.2.18.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">"related_correct_expressions": [
<br class="ltx_break"></span></span>
<span id="A7.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<span id="A7.Ex111"><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex111.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad dm_{water}/dt=-m/\tau\quad\text{(student's expression, correct)}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">=</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(student’s expression, correct)</mtext><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad dm_{water}/dt=-m/\tau\quad\text{(student's expression, correct)},</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
<span id="A7.Ex112"><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex112.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad(M+m(1-t/\tau))\tfrac{dv}{dt}=P-(M+m(1-t/\tau))g," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">g</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad(M+m(1-t/\tau))\tfrac{dv}{dt}=P-(M+m(1-t/\tau))g,</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
<span id="A7.Ex113"><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><span id="A7.Ex113.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  </span><span id="A7.Ex113.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(since escaping water has zero velocity relative to the bucket,the thrust term vanishes)</span></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
<span id="A7.Ex114"><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex114.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad v_{empty}=\tfrac{P\tau}{m}\ln\!\left(\tfrac{M+m}{M}\right)-g\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.748em;" width="0.748em"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ln</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad v_{empty}=\tfrac{P\tau}{m}\ln\!\left(\tfrac{M+m}{M}\right)-g\tau</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.2.19" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.2.19.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> ],
<br class="ltx_break"> "rationale": "The student misapplied the variable-mass form of Newton’s second law: the net external force equal to d/dt(Mv) and thus kept a v dM/dt term on the RHS (or equivalently omitted the momentum-flux term on the RHS), which is incorrect bookkeeping for mass leaving with zero velocity relative to the bucket. For escaping water with velocity equal to the bucket, the relative-velocity term vanishes and the correct ODE is M(t) dv/dt = P - M(t) g, leading to a different integral (logarithmic) result. All subsequent algebra and the final numeric expression therefore follow from this incorrect application."<span id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.2.19.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif">
</span></span></span><pre id="A7.SS3.p5.pic1.2.20" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
}
</pre>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
